    rdf:value """Friday  Mar. 1. 1895 Villa Rosa Fiesole 
Sent off the review of Lafenestre. Maud and I lunched with Loeser and I had tea with Emily - Bernhard called on the Morgans. Began  Richard Feverel  (second time of reading). 
Saturday Mar. 2. 1895 
Rain all day. We finished our German story,  Don Juan von Kolomea .  Mr. and Mrs. Benn came to lunch.
We read Bernhard’s essay on Mohamed in the evening. Finished  R[ichard] Feverel.
Sunday Mar. 3. 95
Began  Einsame Menschen  by Hauptmann. Loeser came to lunch and we had an enchanting walk. The day began with snow, but the afternoon was lovely and we had tea in the garden. Read parts of the Koran in the evening. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 108 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1894-95> .

